Drop the engine's virtual sysroot paths from makedepend's output.

The engine's clang preprocessor reports musl headers under the virtual
clang-VFS sysroot /__unpin_ziglib__/..., which are not real files. makedepend
would record them as Makefile prerequisites and make then dies ("No rule to
make target /__unpin_ziglib__/.../alloca.h"). Filter them in the same sed that
already drops the <built-in>/<command-line> markers; dependency tracking is
irrelevant to a one-shot build. Native only: the cross builds use perl-cross,
which doesn't run makedepend_file.

--- a/makedepend_file.SH
+++ b/makedepend_file.SH
@@ -151,7 +151,7 @@
 	    -e '1d' \
 	    -e '/^#.*<stdin>/d' \
             -e '/^#.*<builtin>/d' \
-            -e '/^#.*<built-in>/d' \
+            -e '/^#.*<built-in>/d' -e '\#/__unpin_ziglib__#d' \
             -e '/^#.*<command line>/d' \
             -e '/^#.*<command-line>/d' \
 	    -e '/^#.*"-"/d' \
